.SH SUBCOMMAND REFERENCE
.SS "\&cps facet list"
\&List facet rules, or show which rule decides each named facet
.PP
.B \&cps facet list [OPTIONS] [FACET]...
.PP
.B Arguments
.TP
.B \&[FACET]...
\&Show the effective value of these facets instead of listing rules
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B \&\-\-root <IMAGE>
\&Image root (default: the running system) [default: /]
.TP
.B \&\-\-package <PACKAGE>
\&Resolve facets for this installed package, including per\-package rules; without FACET arguments, show every facet its actions use
.PP
.B \&\-\-json
.TP
.B \&\-h, \-\-help
\&Print help
.SS "\&cps facet set"
\&Change facet rules for installed package actions
.PP
.B \&cps facet set [OPTIONS] <[PACKAGE:]FACET=true|false|default>...
.PP
.B Arguments
.TP
.B \&<[PACKAGE:]FACET=true|false|default>...
\&FACET, PREFIX.*, or * for the whole image; PACKAGE:FACET or PREFIX/*:FACET for packages; `default` removes the rule
.PP
.B Options
.TP
.B \&\-\-root <IMAGE>
\&Operate on this offline image instead of the running system
.TP
.B \&\-\-config <CONFIG>
\&Distribution configuration of the running system [default: /etc/cps/image.kdl]
.TP
.B \&\-y, \-\-yes
\&Confirm the displayed transaction without prompting
.TP
.B \&\-n, \-\-dry\-run
\&Preview the transaction without applying it
.TP
.B \&\-\-save\-plan <PLAN>
\&Save the exact transaction plan, for `cps status \-\-plan` or a later `cps apply`
.TP
.B \&\-\-no\-recommends
\&Skip recommended packages when resolving the transaction
.TP
.B \&\-\-stage
\&Stage the change in a new Btrfs trial boot environment, or for repair and revert a verified recovery root, instead of changing the running root
.TP
.B \&\-\-with\-dependencies
\&Also apply the PACKAGE:FACET rules to each package's installed dependencies
.TP
.B \&\-h, \-\-help
\&Print help
